    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'ground' is a broad term referring to the solid surface of the earth. While 地盤 (jiban) can mean 'ground' (especially in the sense of the earth's crust or subsoil, or as a foundation), it is a narrower term often implying the quality, stability, or underlying structure of the ground. For a general learner, the most natural and common Japanese word for the general concept of 'ground' (the surface one walks on) is 地面 (jimen). Therefore, 地盤 is semantically narrower and less natural for a general learner in this context.",
